<title>USA: TABLE - Krystal Co Q2 net income rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Krystal Co Q2 net income rises.</headline>
<dateline>CHATTANOOGA, Tenn. 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997		 1996</p>
<p>Second quarter:</p>
<p> Revenues			    $ 63,325,000     $  60,903,000</p>
<p> Net income before items a&amp;b	1,115,000	     764,000</p>
<p> Net income			     1,107,000	     426,000</p>
<p> Net EPS before items			 .15		   .10</p>
<p> Net EPS					  .15		   .06</p>
<p> Average shares			 7,479,000	   7,492,000</p>
<p>SIX MONTHS:</p>
<p> Revenues			     122,488,000	 118,570,000</p>
<p> Net before items a,b &amp; c	   1,517,000	     617,000</p>
<p> Net income (loss)			844,000	   (320,000)</p>
<p> Net EPS before items			 .20		   .08</p>
<p> Net income (loss) per share		.11		 (.04)</p>
<p> Average shares			 7,482,000	   7,507,000</p>
<p>(a)  Reorganization item represents legal and professional</p>
<p>fees and administrative costs incurred in connection with</p>
<p>Chapter 11 proceeding.</p>
<p>(b)  An adjustment, resulting in a reduction in interest expense related to certain pre-petition liabilities, in the amount of $331,000 pre-tax and $205,000 after-tax, or three cents per share, was recorded in the second quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>(c)  Extraordinary item represents write off of unamortized financing costs in conjunction with extinguishment of debt in the amount of $354,000 pre-tax and $220,000 after-tax, or three cents per share, which was recorded in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
</text>
